  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Ethiopia UNICEF WASH Cholera Specialist</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Urban Cholera WASH Coordinator will assess, determine, and coordinate appropriate actions to ensure that the urban water infrastructure is fit for purpose during the current Acute watery diarrhoea and cholera outbreak in Addis Ababa and other major cities. This will include mobilisation of a range of stakeholders, including but not limited to local government, private sector, academics, local and INGOs. This partnership will review the preparedness and response actions taken so far, identify gaps, bottlenecks, immediate and long-term actions if needed. In addition to in-country support, the postholder will benefit from support provided by the WASH and Public Health Emergencies specialist of the East Southern Africa regional office for remote technical support, exchange, info sharing and any other backup that may benefit the objectives.</narrative>
  </description>
